//RS ///
//RS /// A workspace member list (D-JPK-WORKSPACE, `jetpack::WorkspaceFile`)
//RS /// with more than one runnable member (a member whose own entry resolves to a
//RS /// real file, D-ILE1) is an ambiguity naming every member; `-p <member>`
//RS /// picks one explicitly, or the caller can always name a file directly. A
//RS /// plain project (no workspace, or a workspace with exactly zero or one
//RS /// runnable member) resolves exactly like `find_project_entry` always has —
//RS /// no behavior change for the overwhelmingly common single-package case.
//RS ///
//RS /// A declaration-resolved workspace source (D-JPK-WORKSPACE2) is checked at
//RS /// `cwd` directly first —
//RS /// `jetpack::WorkspaceFile::load` never walks upward, matching every
//RS /// other workspace-aware call site — because a monorepo workspace root often
//RS /// carries no `package.jet` of its own (Package facts live entirely in member
//RS /// directories). Only when there's no workspace, or it has zero/one runnable
//RS /// member, does resolution fall back to the ordinary `find_manifest_root` +
//RS /// `find_project_entry` single-package convention (unchanged from before
//RS /// D-CLI-BARE1). Returns `None` outside any package or workspace — the
//RS /// caller keeps today's "no file given" usage error verbatim.
